From 37d25f66d3f730a1d3e12c39f609fb5b5b0faab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:11:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/53] MoE fused gate/up+GLU: publish the Q8_1 at verify
 widths (2-8 tokens) too, per pair under the expert dedup

Each token warp of the fused gate/up+GLU kernel publishes its own rows, routed and shared lanes, at the row index
quantize_q8_1 uses for [ne0, n_used, n_tokens]; counters per (token, lane, group).  Under the expert dedup the owner
warp publishes every pair it computed, with that pair's token and slot.  The down projections find the entries and
skip their quantize_q8_1.  Same quantize arithmetic: bit-identical.  GGML_CUDA_MOE_GLU_Q8_MULTI=0: 1 token only.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh  |  2 +
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq-moe.cu | 80 ++++++++++++++++++----------------
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu     | 22 ++++++----
 3 files changed, 57 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

